[style name="Interaction_Style"]
[background arg="res://assets/images/Intro/MeetingWGod-IntroScene2.jpg" fade="0.0"]
God: I see you've returned from your journey.
God: Now lets see what fate altering decisions you've made.
[background arg="res://assets/images/Intro/Half_shale.jpg" fade="0.0"]
join Scale center [animation="Instant In"]
God: You've helped a lost companion out of the goodwill of your heart.
set {Scale_value} += 1
jump Change_scale
if {Whiskers.Accepted_Fish_Quest} == true:
	God: You offered food to someone in need, that's good deed.
	set {Scale_value} += 1
elif {Whiskers.Shoo_away} == true:
	God: You refused to feed a cat even tho it wouldn't have cost you anything.
	God: Not only that, but you were mean to him.
	set {Scale_value} -= 2
else:
	God: You ignored a cry for food.
	set {Scale_value} -= 1
jump Change_scale
if {Hugo.Followed_to_rockfall} == true:
	God: You've accepted Hugo's kindness following him to Rockfall.
	set {Scale_value} += 1
else:
	God: You've ignored Hugo's kindness and tought you were better off alone.
jump Change_scale
if {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} == 1:
	God: You tried your best to save Ian's suffering soul, but failed in the end.
elif {Ian.Selected_Ian_Choice} == 2:
	God: You did your job as a doctor. You gave Ian his last mercy, but you did take a life.
	set {Scale_value} += 1
else:
	God: You were mean to a dying person, and refused to help.
	set {Scale_value} -= 2
jump Change_scale
if {Malrik.Trusted_malric} == true:
	God: Even when warned about Marlic you decided to trust him and not the rumours.
	set {Scale_value} += 2
else:
	God: You blindly based your trust on groundless rumours and didn't give Marlic a chance.
	God: On top of that, you stole his book behind his back.
	set {Scale_value} -= 2
jump Change_scale
if {Dead_person_choice} == 1:
	God: You've managed to save all 5 lives, which sadly came at the cost of Vivian's.
	set {Scale_value} += 4
	jump Change_scale
	if {Blame_choice} == 1:
		God: You pretentiously accepted credit for something in what Malric also played a part.
		set {Scale_value} -= 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 2:
		God: You were honest about who helped you, but that cost you some credibility with those who don't trust Malric.
	elif {Blame_choice} == 3:
		God: You pretentiously accepted credit for something in what Malric also played a part. At least you thanked him in private.
		set {Scale_value} -= 1
	jump Change_scale
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 2:
	God: You took the life of a criminal, yet it left four dead.
	set {Scale_value} -= 3
	if {Blame_choice} == 1:
		God: You were brave and stood by your mistake.
		God: You even shouldered the whole blame, shielding Malric from further disgrace.
		set {Scale_value} += 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 2:
		God: You put the blame of your own wrongdoings on Malric.
		set {Scale_value} -= 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 3:
		God: You didn't fulfill your duty as a doctor, and you hold a grudge over your own mistake.
		set {Scale_value} -= 2
	jump Change_scale
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 3:
	God: You took the life of an innocent, yet it left two more dead.
	if {Blame_choice} == 1:
		God: You were brave and stood by your choices.
		set {Scale_value} += 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 2:
		God: You put the blame of your own wrongdoings on Malric.
		set {Scale_value} -= 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 3:
		God: You only half fulfilled your duty as a doctor, and you hold a grudge over your own mistake.
		set {Scale_value} -= 2
	jump Change_scale
elif {Dead_person_choice} == 4:
	God: You let five people die. Altough no one was sacrificed.
	set {Scale_value} -= 2
	if {Blame_choice} == 1:
		God: You made the effort to find the cure.
		God: You could've faulted Malric, but you kept his involvement to yourself.
		set {Scale_value} += 2
	elif {Blame_choice} == 2:
		God: You've kept your reputation with the village intact at the cost of Malric's unjust exposure.
	jump Change_scale

if {Scale_value} == 0:
	God: Your scale is once again balanced, you are doing an astonishing job of being neutral.
	God: But one memory could never have been enough to determine your fate. Lives are put together by a lifetime's worth of memories.
	God: You shall be tested in your next one.
	
elif {Scale_value} < 0:
	God: I see that you have taken the first dip towards the negative end.
	God: but fear not Thorinn it's impossible to grasp someone's nature just with one memory, thus you still get plenty of chances to redeem yourself.

else:
	God: Your choices have been going in the right direction.
	God: you just have to keep following this oath, because one memory could never be enough to determine your fate.
	God: Lives are put together by a lifetime's worth of memories. You shall be tested in your next one.

[end_timeline]
label Change_scale
if {Scale_value} == 0:
	update Scale (Neutral)
	[wait time="0.3" hide_text="false"]

elif {Scale_value} > 0:
	update Scale (Neutral)
	[wait time="0.3" hide_text="false"]
	update Scale (Good)
elif {Scale_value} < 0:
	update Scale (Neutral)
	[wait time="0.3" hide_text="false"]
	update Scale (Bad)
return
